  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Taposh Sikandar And 2 Others vs State Of U.P. on 19 March, 2021 Author: Pankaj Bhatia Bench: Pankaj Bhatia High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 77 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 12617 of 2021 Applicant :- Taposh Sikandar And 2 Others Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Anand Kumar Singh",
    "facts": "The present bail application has been filed by the applicants with a prayer to enlarge them on bail in Case Crime No. 53 of 2021, under Sections 188, 269, 273 of IPC, Section 3 Epidemic Act, Section 5/15 Environment Act and Section 31 (1) Food Safety Standard Act, Police Station Lanka, District Varanasi.",
    "arguments": "Counsel for the applicants argues that the applicants are labourer and have been falsely implicated. He further submits that the applicants are in custody since 19.1.2021 and have no criminal antecedents, which fact has not been denied by the learned AGA. He further submitted that there is no possibility of the applicants' fleeing away from the judicial process or tampering with the Taposh Sikandar And 2 Others vs State Of U.P. on 19 March, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/34286251/ 1 prosecution evidence or witnesses and, in case, the applicants are enlarged on bail, the applicants shall not misuse the liberty of bail. There is nothing on record to demonstrate that if the applicants are enlarged on bail, it would adversely affect the trial of the case. Per contra, learned A.G.A. has opposed the bail prayer of the applicants.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Counsel for the applicants argues that the applicants are labourer and have been falsely implicated. He further submits that the applicants are in custody since 19.1.2021 and have no criminal antecedents, which fact has not been denied by the learned AGA. He further submitted that there is no possibility of the applicants' fleeing away from the judicial process or tampering with the Taposh Sikandar And 2 Others vs State Of U.P. on 19 March, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/34286251/",
    "respondent_arguments": "1 prosecution evidence or witnesses and, in case, the applicants are enlarged on bail, the applicants shall not misuse the liberty of bail. There is nothing on record to demonstrate that if the applicants are enlarged on bail, it would adversely affect the trial of the case. Per contra, learned A.G.A. has opposed the bail prayer of the applicants.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
